---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ToConfirm from '../components/ToConfirm.astro';
import { site } from '../site.config';
import { url } from '../lib/url';
---

<Base title={`Safeguarding | ${site.name}`} description="How My Maths Mentor sessions are arranged and how children are kept safe.">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <span class="kicker">Keeping children safe</span>
      <h1>Safeguarding</h1>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="container container--narrow prose">
    <ToConfirm>
      <p>
        This page is a framework only. Every arrangement below needs confirming, and only checks that have been verified
        should be published.
      </p>
    </ToConfirm>

    <p class="lede">
      Your child’s safety and wellbeing come first. This page explains how sessions are arranged and what you can
      expect.
    </p>

    <h2>Where sessions take place</h2>
    <p>
      Sessions take place in person at {site.owner}’s home in {site.locality}. The full address is shared privately
      with parents and carers when sessions are arranged, and is never published online.
    </p>

    <h2>Checks and background</h2>
    <p>
      {site.owner} is an engineering lecturer in further education, with a degree in Mechanical Engineering.
    </p>
    <ToConfirm>
      <p>DBS check: the type of check, when it was issued and whether it’s on the DBS Update Service.</p>
    </ToConfirm>
    <ToConfirm>
      <p>Insurance: whether public liability (and any professional) insurance is in place.</p>
    </ToConfirm>

    <h2>Parents and carers</h2>
    <ToConfirm>
      <p>
        Whether a parent or carer stays during sessions or nearby, how drop-off and collection work, and what happens if
        a child is unwell or upset during a session.
      </p>
    </ToConfirm>

    <h2>Photos and personal information</h2>
    <p>
      Photos of children are never taken or shared without permission from a parent or carer. The enquiry form doesn’t
      ask for children’s names, dates of birth or medical details.
    </p>

    <h2>Raising a concern</h2>
    <ToConfirm>
      <p>
        How parents can raise a concern, the safeguarding training {site.owner} has completed, and how a concern about a
        child would be reported.
      </p>
    </ToConfirm>
    <p>If you think a child is in immediate danger, call 999.</p>

    <p><a href={url('/')}>Back to the home page</a></p>
  </div>
</Base>
